# QA replay of older What's New cards' previews (drafted in the UI QA re-check of the grid's fixes, 2026-10-26): one
# line of each kind pointed at, from one to the next as a pointer moves down the card, one still each: the previews that
# stage a map of their own (replay, extracts, joined, leaders) inside the grid's strips, and those that lay only a plate
# or a cue over the player's map (clock, stash, notes), each over the player's map put back (DESIGN.md §4, *What's New*:
# "leaving puts the map back as it was"). A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and
# what each still must show: whatsnew-previews.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first.
tour end
# The player's map is Customs, read once, so a preview staged there has its map at once.
map customs
wait 3
whatsnew 0.4.0
wait 1.5
whatsnew 0.4.0 2
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\replay
whatsnew 0.4.0 3
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\extracts
whatsnew 0.4.0 4
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\clock
whatsnew 0.4.0 5
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\joined
whatsnew 0.5.0 1
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\stash
whatsnew 0.6.0 2
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\notes
whatsnew 0.6.2 1
wait 2.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\leaders
whatsnew leave
wait 1.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-previews\end
exit
